course: dictionary
lesson: 1113
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and bray is one of them. The clues in the sentence show you which meaning the writer chose. «Donkeys bray to call other donkeys.» Here bray is the loud, harsh hee-haw sound a donkey makes.
explain: «Her braying laugh filled the whole classroom.» There is no donkey in this sentence, so look for a different meaning. A braying laugh is loud and unpleasant, so here bray describes a person who laughs or talks loudly in an annoying way.
explain: Check your choice by swapping in your meaning. Does «the donkey's loud bray» make sense? Yes. Does «her loud, unpleasant laugh» fit the second sentence? Yes. If your meaning does not fit, try the other one.
fact: Bray can be a verb or a noun: a donkey brays, and the donkey's bray is the sound.
fact: «Bray» means the loud, harsh hee-haw noise of a donkey.
fact: «Braying» can also describe people who laugh or talk loudly and unpleasantly.
fact: «Real donkeys are mostly quiet, but a bray can be heard about three kilometres away.»
fact: The «hee» of a donkey's bray is breathed in, and the «haw» is breathed out.
exercise: «Donkeys bray to call other donkeys.» What does bray mean here? | To run very fast across the desert | *To make a loud, harsh donkey noise | To laugh loudly and unpleasantly | To sleep in a stable
exercise: «Her braying laugh filled the whole classroom.» What does braying suggest? | *Loud and unpleasant | A donkey in a field | Quiet and gentle | Soft and sleepy
exercise: A donkey's bray can be heard about three kilometres away. What is the bray? | *The sound a donkey makes | A laugh | A field | A sleep
test: «The donkey gave a loud bray in the stable.» Which meaning fits? | Quiet whispering | A stone wall | *The donkey's noise | A person's happy song
test: Why is context important for the word bray? | *Because bray has more than one meaning, so the sentence shows which one | Because donkeys never make any noise | Because bray means only one thing | Because bray is always a noun
exam: «Real donkeys are mostly quiet, but their bray is so loud it carries about three kilometres.» What does bray mean in this sentence? | A type of food | A kind of hat | Walking slowly across the sand | *The loud sound a donkey makes
